{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788328062339412001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"intensive-messy-zethuswasp","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"db18dc01055a25694a4e712918cfc42d9a8d78466637953541ee9266ad557382","event_uuid":"66aedfb1-69fe-4ad6-acb0-3f94cfb17b06","position":{"commit_sha":"bd31df29b723c9e84e6e352e716f881975a74696","position":"1788314549167033001-66aedfb1-69fe-4ad6-acb0-3f94cfb17b06"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8e8d3ee9ad3df215f6d0d5a558c78ee9d2f6ecd397c896d778e9030dd216b1c7","event_uuid":"34776ae2-6ccb-4353-857e-65b5b9a68cfa","position":{"commit_sha":"8495e7d3abcba14635df5f1f3b7b263fd5d954f5","position":"1788314569642917001-34776ae2-6ccb-4353-857e-65b5b9a68cfa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"44e0f3c3715267fa73526880e67f443d03c664f9e78f4bd7b187d70debe2a005","event_uuid":"594895cf-a21a-48b5-b600-1906d6d8cf9b","position":{"commit_sha":"6ab67229e04b3edd6aac42b7c052b9abf621a60b","position":"1788314957919647001-594895cf-a21a-48b5-b600-1906d6d8cf9b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788314549167033001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"594895cf-a21a-48b5-b600-1906d6d8cf9b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"86c0-59ec-a28b-4f7c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPrivate re-exports, wrappers, and alias assignments survive after ownership moved elsewhere. Their only beneficiaries are repository imports, strings, and monkeypatch targets, so they create a second binding without protecting a public compatibility contract. The approved policy requires every such consumer to migrate and prohibits new internal-only shims.\n\n## Approach\n\nA prerequisite ADR establishes the boundary and enforcement policy. After it merges, disjoint children migrate all source, tests, dynamic imports, string lookups, and monkeypatch consumers by subsystem and delete the old binding. Public facades, MCP wire schemas, event readers, and persisted-data migrations remain separate contracts.\n\n## Child Decomposition\n\n- The ADR child performs RESEARCH, DRAFT, HOLD, and MERGE for the no-internal-shim rule.\n- Core/reconciler, CLI/security/graph/grounding, and LLM/workflow/MCP-model children own disjoint migration censuses.\n- The LLM/workflow shard also owns approved SDC3 alias migrations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A merged ADR defines one canonical binding after private moves, atomic consumer migration, valid exceptions, and recurrence prevention.\n- [ ] Every enumerated internal shim has its semantic/static and string/dynamic/monkeypatch consumers moved to its canonical owner.\n- [ ] No old private binding remains solely for internal compatibility.\n- [ ] Deliberate public facades, wire schemas, event readers, and persisted-data migrations retain their independently specified contracts.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","86c0-59ec-a28b-4f7c"],["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change on this container: the ADR and disjoint implementation children own all policy and code edits. Where evidence lives: child Gerrit changes, direct consumer censuses, and completion-verifier records establish the end state.","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","architecture","compatibility","internal-shims"],"ticket_id":"6640-ac11-5c55-46b5","ticket_type":"story","title":"Eliminate internal-only compatibility shims under an ADR-governed policy","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["66aedfb1-69fe-4ad6-acb0-3f94cfb17b06","34776ae2-6ccb-4353-857e-65b5b9a68cfa","594895cf-a21a-48b5-b600-1906d6d8cf9b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788328062339412001,"uuid":"22cb855c-621e-4d7c-9d18-9038a270565e"}